# Subagent Model Selection

When launching subagents via the `Task` tool, always set the `model` parameter.
Default (inheriting the parent model) is wasteful: expensive reasoning models do
simple file reads; cheap fast models stall on complex code generation.

## Model roster

_Last verified: 2026-06-19. See **Maintenance** section below before trusting this table._

| Slug | Strength | Cost/speed |
|---|---|---|
| `gpt-5.3-codex` | Code writing, editing, refactoring | Fast, cheap |
| `composer-2.5-fast` | Read-only exploration, simple searches | Fastest, cheapest |
| `composer-2.5` | General-purpose, moderate reasoning | Balanced |
| `claude-4.6-sonnet-medium-thinking` | Planning, architecture, analysis | Medium |
| `claude-4.6-opus-max` | Deep review, security audit, complex synthesis | Slow, expensive |
| `claude-opus-4-8-thinking-high` | Deep reasoning, complex synthesis, high-stakes analysis | Slowest, most expensive |
| `gpt-5.3-codex-xhigh` | Hard refactors and deeper code reasoning | Slower, higher cost |
| `gpt-5.4-high` | Strong general-purpose reasoning and synthesis | Slower, premium |
| `gpt-5.5-medium` | Strong general reasoning with better speed balance | Medium-fast, mid-high cost |

## Assignment rules

| Subagent type | Model to use |
|---|---|
| `explore` (read-only codebase exploration) | `composer-2.5-fast` |
| `shell` (running commands, git operations) | `composer-2.5-fast` |
| `generalPurpose` writing/editing code | `gpt-5.3-codex` |
| `generalPurpose` planning / analysis | `composer-2.5` |
| `bugbot` / `security-review` | `claude-4.6-opus-max` |
| `best-of-n-runner` (isolated code experiments) | `gpt-5.3-codex` |

## Do / Don't

```
✅ task("Explore the auth module", subagent_type="explore", model="composer-2.5-fast")
✅ task("Refactor the checkout tool", subagent_type="generalPurpose", model="gpt-5.3-codex")
✅ task("Plan the caching strategy", subagent_type="generalPurpose", model="composer-2.5")
❌ Omitting `model` (inherits parent — often overkill for the subtask)
❌ Using claude-4.6-opus-max for a simple file search
❌ Using composer-2.5-fast for a nuanced architecture decision
```

## Escalation

If a subagent returns an incomplete or incorrect result, re-run with one tier
higher. Document the escalation reason in the agent journal.

## Maintenance

The model roster comes from Cursor's system prompt (the `Task` tool description),
not from this repo. It changes when Cursor updates its model offerings.

**Every agent that reads this rule must:**
1. Compare the slugs above against the available model slugs listed in its own
   `Task` tool description (visible in the system context).
2. If they differ — new slugs present, old slugs missing — update the roster
   table, update the _Last verified_ date, add a `CHANGELOG.md` entry, and
   append an `agent-journal.md` entry before proceeding.
3. Never use a slug that does not appear in the current `Task` tool description;
   the call will silently fall back to the default model.
